  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is clearly the strongest RNA encoder (0.7062–0.7150 in multimodal vs. 0.6352–0.6390 for pca_n2000), and the current best config (042) pairs scvi_n200 with imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and concat. However, we have no data on how well scvi_n200 performs as a standalone RNA-only model. config_006 shows pca_n2000 rna_only at 0.5907, but the jump from pca to scvi in the multimodal setting was ~4–7%, so the RNA-only ceiling with scvi is unknown. Question: config_048 (scvi_n200, rna_only, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation against config_001 (same RNA encoder, aggregation, profile; only the image modality is removed). It directly quantifies the marginal contribution of the image modality when the RNA representation is strong. Why best next experiment: If scvi_n200 rna_only approaches ~0.68–0.70, the image adds little and further multimodal tuning has diminishing returns, redirecting budget toward RNA encoder improvements (e.g., scgpt) or profile settings. If it drops to ~0.60–0.63, the image modality is essential and we should continue exploiting the multimodal direction. Either way, this single experiment resolves a major architectural uncertainty that would otherwise cloud every subsequent comparison, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

